  nonce: b018  # b018
  message: "DONE in PR #1902 (merged 0cb6bd3f16). Deliverables:\n- The classification table: docs/surveys/axiom-falsifiability.md. All 19 declared axioms are classed as testable, partly testable or needing per-row judgment, with the reason. For the judgment ones it records what a reviewer samples.\n- The tests: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_axiom_falsification.py and packages/hypergumbo-lang-extended1/tests/test_axiom_falsification_extended1.py.\n- Filed falsifications: WI-sukug (evidence label set by resolution in 8 of 12 languages) and WI-gisip (visibility defaults to public in every language).\n- Filed rulings: WI-mupal (what a route marker represents) and WI-kuzoh (ADR-0050 does not cover two-crossing simultaneous rows).\n- Found in passing: WI-fanad (ruby drops a call on an externally typed local).\n- A note on INV-fuhin (the ecosystem half).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-run on merged dev 0cb6bd3f16 via smart-test: 84 passed, 18 xfailed, 102 collected. All 18 are strict xfails naming an item, so each fix makes its test XPASS and fail the suite until the mark is removed:\n- 8 WI-sukug;\n- 5 WI-gisip;\n- 1 each WI-higik, INV-fuhin, WI-dagun, WI-savoh, WI-zakil.\n\nMutation controls, before merge, in a detached worktree with a pinned PYTHONPATH: eight production mutations turned 43 tests red. They were visibility default, post-pass reason, directness stamp, unresolved label, .ts language, java receiver key, kind rewrite and a tier listed twice. The checker controls and the verify-claims reach controls stayed green. Two mutations left one test each green: Python's own unresolved emitter is not the shared one, and TS's kind concept is analyzer-stamped, not enrichment-stamped. The survey and commit say so.\n\nNot done here:\n- ADR-0050 'same medium across catalogues', which needs a hand-written medium map (judgment).\n- An entrypoint-kind metamorphic test, which needs one entrypoint detectable two ways.\n- ADR-0061 ruling 7.\n- Reproducing WI-kufos on a fixture.\nEach is recorded as a gap in the survey."  # b018
